{
  "esm": "0.6.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "duo_subdivide_fold",
    "description": "DUO icosahedral build-time level-fold (RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §7.3; bead esd-heg.4). The full level-N mesh expressed declaratively as the base icosahedron seed folded through the one-level value-invention refine pass (subdivide_refine.esm) N times, where N = grid options.level is a build-time constant. This document declares the SEED as a literal/trivial FAQ constant: (1) vert_raw — the 12 golden-ratio (phi = (1+sqrt(5))/2) icosahedron vertices, pre-normalization (value-free parameter shape; concrete data fed by the conformance harness, mirroring subdivide_refine.esm); (2) seed_sq — the squared norm of each raw vertex, reduced over space (sum_product FAQ); (3) seed_coord — the unit-sphere base vertices = vert_raw / sqrt(seed_sq) (the normalize-to-sphere FAQ; the level-0 mesh vertices), bit-for-bit identical to the imperative _icosahedron_vertices; (4) face_vert — the 20 base triangular faces (CONST connectivity), the seed connectivity consumed by the first refine pass. THE FOLD: the level-N vertex/face index sets are obtained by chaining subdivide_refine over (seed_coord, face_vert): each pass's output vertices+faces become the next pass's input parameters (vert_coord, face_vert). This is exactly the per-level driver loop `for _ in 1:level` of _subdivide_icosahedron (src/grids/duo.jl) — the last recursive kernel — expressed as a composition of declarative passes. ESS has no native build-time repeat/iterate/fold construct over a build-time-constant level (no such key in esm-schema.json; no whole-model value-invention runner), so the N-times unroll is performed caller-side, exactly as the landed precedent test/test_duo_subdivision_faq.jl drives the single pass; the missing native affordance is filed as ESS bead ess-vnk. Value-free structural spec; index sizes are the canonical level-0 seed (Nv=12, Nc=20). Byte/numeric equivalence to the imperative _subdivide_icosahedron across the level ladder (L=0,1,2) is proven by test/test_duo_subdivision_fold.jl: byte-identical canonical faces, icos_level{0,1,2} counts (20*4^L cells), imperative coords to ULP.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciDiscretizations/gastown.furiosa"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "duo",
      "icosahedral",
      "subdivision",
      "level-fold",
      "value-invention",
      "seed",
      "faq",
      "esd-heg.4"
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "IcosahedralSeed": {
      "index_sets": {
        "verts": {
          "kind": "interval",
          "size": 12
        },
        "faces": {
          "kind": "interval",
          "size": 20
        },
        "corners": {
          "kind": "interval",
          "size": 3
        },
        "space": {
          "kind": "interval",
          "size": 3
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "vert_raw": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [
            "verts",
            "space"
          ],
          "description": "Raw (pre-normalization) cartesian coordinates of the 12 base icosahedron vertices: entries drawn from {0, +/-1, +/-phi} with phi = (1+sqrt(5))/2 the golden ratio. The literal/trivial FAQ seed constant (value-free shape; the concrete {0,+/-1,+/-phi} layout is fed by the harness)."
        },
        "face_vert": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [
            "faces",
            "corners"
          ],
          "description": "Vertex ids (1-based) of each of the 20 base icosahedron triangular faces, outward-wound. The seed connectivity (CONST) consumed by the first refine pass of the fold."
        },
        "seed_sq": {
          "type": "state",
          "shape": [
            "verts"
          ],
          "description": "Squared norm of each raw vertex, reduced over space (sum_product FAQ): seed_sq[v] = sum_d vert_raw[v,d]^2."
        },
        "seed_coord": {
          "type": "state",
          "shape": [
            "verts",
            "space"
          ],
          "description": "Unit-sphere base icosahedron vertex coordinates = vert_raw / sqrt(seed_sq) (normalize-to-sphere FAQ). The level-0 mesh vertices; the seed of the build-time fold. Bit-for-bit identical to the imperative _icosahedron_vertices."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "_comment": "(seed-1) seed_sq[v] = sum_d vert_raw[v,d]^2 (squared norm; sum_product over space). Squares are products (*), NOT ^, so the float ops match the imperative `n = sqrt(v[1]^2+v[2]^2+v[3]^2)` bit-for-bit (Julia v^2 lowers to v*v).",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "seed_sq",
              "v"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "args": [
              "vert_raw"
            ],
            "semiring": "sum_product",
            "output_idx": [
              "v"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "v": {
                "from": "verts"
              },
              "d": {
                "from": "space"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "vert_raw",
                    "v",
                    "d"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "vert_raw",
                    "v",
                    "d"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "(seed-2) seed_coord[v,d] = vert_raw[v,d] / sqrt(seed_sq[v]) — the normalize-to-sphere FAQ. The level-0 base icosahedron vertex; the seed of the fold. sqrt(seed_sq[v]) reproduces the single imperative `n` per vertex, so each component divides by the identical norm bit-for-bit.",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "seed_coord",
              "v",
              "d"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "args": [
              "vert_raw",
              "seed_sq"
            ],
            "semiring": "sum_product",
            "output_idx": [
              "v",
              "d"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "v": {
                "from": "verts"
              },
              "d": {
                "from": "space"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "vert_raw",
                    "v",
                    "d"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "sqrt",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "seed_sq",
                        "v"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
